    <briefdescription>
<para>Bump-pointer arena for monomial storage, backed by a <computeroutput><ref refid="classmemt_1_1_arena" kindref="compound">memt::Arena</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Hands out contiguous <computeroutput><ref refid="classint" kindref="compound">int</ref></computeroutput> ranges via <computeroutput>alloc(size)</computeroutput> (returns <computeroutput>[<ref refid="ringelem_8cpp_a7dc3f254421434195d252afe59ba8dac_1a7dc3f254421434195d252afe59ba8dac" kindref="member">begin</ref>, <ref refid="ringelem_8cpp_a9e12da0d68ca4715109c3198cbe62a66_1a9e12da0d68ca4715109c3198cbe62a66" kindref="member">end</ref>)</computeroutput>). Supports LIFO <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space_ab3ba4d3a536186667fbb01c243b301e2_1ab3ba4d3a536186667fbb01c243b301e2" kindref="member">popLastAlloc</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space_a7caac63a4c3d9bdb21ff4e07acd2c1e4_1a7caac63a4c3d9bdb21ff4e07acd2c1e4" kindref="member">shrinkLastAlloc</ref></computeroutput> so a monomial can be allocated at its maximum length, written in place, then trimmed <mdash/> the pattern the variable-size <computeroutput>Collection</computeroutput> classes use for intern-or-pop. The whole arena is reset with <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space_aee5cf1d291edd4a7ce1ff315b598585d_1aee5cf1d291edd4a7ce1ff315b598585d" kindref="member">freeAllAllocs</ref></computeroutput> or released to the OS with <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space_a0ad272aa353399ef786ba2054ad0ab80_1a0ad272aa353399ef786ba2054ad0ab80" kindref="member">freeAllAllocsAndBackingMemory</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
